WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:04.471
Iceland is full of stories.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.176
As a National Geographic

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.413
photographer,
I voyage across the circumpolar Arctic,

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.449
immersing myself
in some of the most raw yet

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.985
beautiful places on the planet.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.789
For this adventure,
I'm exploring Iceland in winter.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.126
This time of year,
the land is covered in darkness.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.930
I'm on a journey to find the rare glimpses
of light in the midst of that darkness

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.600
that revealed
just how incredible this place is.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.240
Thousands of winters
are written into Iceland's glaciers,

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.476
embedded into each layer of ice as it is
formed

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.280
in the low light of evening.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.949
I walk deep into the glacier's heart.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.285
I'm traveling through time.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:57.590
The most ancient ice is the clearest
and bluest.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.360
The color and shape is what draws me in.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.530
As the dim evening light

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.567
turns to complete darkness,
I come upon a wrecked DC-3 airplane

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:11.905
from decades ago, revealed by the
light of the aurora borealis.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.781
The darkness recedes just

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.517
enough to see the landscapes
take shape again.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.923
The small northern island,

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.525
with its fresh volcanic landscape,

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:35.128
is full of the push
and pull of mighty forces.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.264
Mountains
rise out of the sea in dramatic shape.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.936
And where water touches Earth,
it becomes a sculptor,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.239
drawing tracks and trails as it cascades

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:49.109
across the volcanic rocks.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.511
As the light of the sun begins
to appear again,

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.514
my journey has come full circle.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.684
The light that reaches my camera's
eye is just a few photons,

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:02.288
but those photons are a million years old,
and they speak to me.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:04.691
That's just it.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.026
The darkness slows me down.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.062
The photographic process slows me down,

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.232
enough to listen to the stories
that the land has to tell.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.902
Free of professional kit
and lighting and crew,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:20.106
it's just me
and the Oppo Find X5 Pro, listening.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:24.577
And when I've learned to listen, each
photograph transcends a single moment,

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:29.415
a window into the past
that illuminates our vision of the future.

